  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">ENHANCED MECHANISMS FOR THE PROVISION OF PROTECTION AND ASSISTANCE FOR VICTIMS OF TRAFFICKING IN SRI LANKA</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">This project will look to sustain the efforts of the National Anti-Human Trafficking Force to increase its capacity to identify victims of trafficking and provide them with appropriate assistance and protection. The government shelter established under a previous J/TIP-funded project will be reinforced through capacity building programs for its staff and resources for its management. The project will also look to train and build the capacity of the Sri Lanka Bureau of Foreign Employment (SLBFE) and its staff at overseas missions including labor attaches and other consular staff, the staff of the Department of Labor and Ministry of External Affairs. The project will also develop a victim identification and referral mechanisms for use by the staff of these entities. At present the SLBFE operates short-term shelters in certain labor receiving countries in the Middle East and an overnight shelter close to the Katunayake International Airport for returning Sri Lankan female migrants who have encountered abuse abroad. This project will train and sensitize shelter staff on TIP victim identification techniques and on procedures for providing appropriate assistance and protection services to victims.</narrative>
  </description>
